                <pb facs="0408" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg348"/>

                <head>No. 2.</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Vessel wanted.</hi></p>
                <p>By authority of the Board of Immigration, the undersigned solicits proposals for
                    furnishing a schooner or other vessel, of sufficient capacity to accommodate at
                    least fortyimmigrant passengers. Such vessel will be required to proceed to the
                    Gilbert and Caroline Islands and such other points as may be designated by the
                    board, or the agentwho may be selected to take charge of the enterprise.
                    Proposals will be received until the first day of September next. Further
                    information may be obtained by application to</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FERD. W. HUTCHINSON, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >President.</hi></signed><lb/><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bureau of Immigration</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 25, 1868</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
